@MichalStrehovsky - is the resource stripping just for framework code, or does it also extend to user authored code?

@brianrob @davmason  - do either of you know of any scenarios where localized resources for Framework authored EventSources are important? My first instinct is that we should only localize messages that have a decent chance of being observed by application users, but ETW events are almost exclusively viewed by app developers. I did a search and found only 9 localized event name strings in the runtime repo not including test code. 5 are for TPL events, the other 4 are copies of the 'OperationReturnedSomething'* event on the various Private.InternalDiagnostics.System.Net.Xyz EventSources. 

*yes that is the literal name of the event in the code :)
